.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_REPLACE_RANGES 3 2026-11-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_replace_ranges \- replace fixed-size ranges in a named staged MPQ member
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.B typedef struct mpq_update_replace_range {
.B "    libmpq__off_t offset;"
.B "    const uint8_t *data;"
.B "    size_t size;"
.B } mpq_update_replace_range_s;
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_replace_ranges("
.BI "        mpq_update_s *" "update,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        const mpq_update_replace_range_s *" "ranges,"
.BI "        size_t " "range_count"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Selects a member using the same first-hit lookup as
libmpq__update_replace_data(3). Use libmpq__update_replace_ranges_identity(3)
for a particular locale/platform tuple or an eligible shared classic row.
.PP
Each descriptor holds a zero-based logical offset, a data pointer and a
byte count. Offsets refer to the member at the start of this call. Ranges
can overlap or arrive in any order. Later entries override earlier ones.
The logical length remains fixed. NULL data is valid for a zero-length
range. NULL ranges is valid with a zero count. The array and payload bytes
are borrowed until the call returns.
.PP
An empty batch and a batch of valid zero-length ranges preserve the current
stage and signatures. A nonempty batch preserves untouched plaintext,
encryption, KEY, supported storage and checksum policies, and FILETIME.
Lossless tagged compression can use a different method. File integrity
metadata is regenerated under the archive's current policy. Existing
signatures are invalidated under the ordinary update rules.
.PP
Sectorized data is read and re-encoded in bounded payload buffers, with
separate sector metadata and range-plan allocations. SINGLE uses full-unit
buffers. Existing candidate reconstruction can copy unrelated packed members.
.PP
Lossy ADPCM sectors, physical patch and delete members, managed internal
members, and ambiguous or unsupported layouts are rejected. Embedded and MPQE
updates retain their existing eligibility and publication rules. High-offset
MPQ v2 extents beyond the transaction implementation's 32-bit limit are
rejected for nonempty range replacements.
.PP
Commit alone publishes the candidate. A failure before adoption preserves the
previous stage. Qualifying failures during adoption leave the update
abort-only. See libmpq__update_commit(3) and libmpq__update_abort(3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fB0\fP on success or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates a missing argument or live identity.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_SEEK indicates a negative range offset.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE indicates a range outside the member, unrepresentable
capacity, or an unsupported size or extent.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT indicates an unsupported representation or ambiguous
identity. LIBMPQ_ERROR_READ also covers checksum or validation mismatches.
Allocation, decryption, codec and I/O errors are reported by the transaction.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3),
.BR libmpq__update_replace_ranges_identity (3)
